WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.175
Some tasks let one person take over an
identity or open data to the wrong people,

2
00:00:05.175 --> 00:00:08.250
and the platform can't stop
the misuse on its own.

3
00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:12.021
For those, the program requires
two approvers besides the

4
00:00:12.021 --> 00:00:15.950
person doing the work, both
recorded before anyone elevates.

5
00:00:15.950 --> 00:00:20.320
The list is short: resets on accounts
the desk can't normally touch,

6
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.204
repairing a cloud account's
link to its on-premises record,

7
00:00:24.204 --> 00:00:28.250
restoring accounts outside the
HR process, and bulk changes.

8
00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.868
The second approver checks that
the requester was verified,

9
00:00:31.868 --> 00:00:34.400
the change is exact,
and the urgency is real.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.925
A caller pressing for speed
goes to the emergency process.

11
00:00:37.925 --> 00:00:41.550
The decision: never waive the
second approver for urgency.

12
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.580
Next, third-party apps.
